{
  "rationale": "The design separates sensing and actuation in the plant, then uses deterministic specifications to map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe motion choice. Clear-space exploration is biased toward coverage by defaulting to random_walk, with a short forward pulse only after a clear observation. Obstacle events always force entry into dedicated turn-recovery states, and path_clear returns quickly to exploration. Action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear so uncontrollables are processed before the intended one-shot controllable pulse, while safety-critical obstacle events still preempt.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use a sensor plant for uncontrollable perception outcomes and a motion plant for controllable pulse actions",
    "Use one policy specification with clear, forward-progress, and obstacle-recovery states so every obstacle passes through a turn state before exploration resumes"
  ],
